    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `timezone` field to the Owner response, an IANA name derived from the owner's locality/region via a fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nThe logic is placed where it belongs, reusing existing patterns:\n\n1. **`util/Timezones.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility util holding the fixed region-to-IANA-timezone table, mirroring the existing `CityRegions` class. Returns `null` for regions with no known timezone (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `timezone(owner)` mapping method that derives the value from the owner's existing `locality(owner)` (the region), delegating the lookup to `Timezones.of(...)`. This reuses the locality derivation rather than recomputing the region.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` property to the Owner schema (right after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` passes (Sydney \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`), and the full suite builds green.",
